-- §3  Every denominator the corpus leans on, and what it sits under.
# One row per (kind, denominator), with how many claims carry it and what they are filed on.
#
# `week` and `semana` are two denominators
#   Not one. That is the entire argument for pm:StatedDenominator: a `LIKE` reads a denominator
#   out of free text and silently decides the Portuguese token is the English one. Here they are
#   separate rows because a filer wrote each of them.
#
# `each` is not `period`
#   `GPU-hour per GPU` carries a denominator that is not a cycle, which is the case a string
#   search cannot see and a typed element cannot miss.
-- units/denominators.sqlc, the census over every claim carrying one.
SELECT d.kind          AS "kind!",
       d.denominator   AS "denominator!",
       d.claims        AS "claims!",
       d.filed_on      AS "filed_on!"
FROM (
    :compose(units/denominators.sqlc)
) d
ORDER BY d.kind, d.claims DESC
